  "identity": "svt_pp_of_book == 100 x reach x exposure x hazard, exactly. `reach` is accounts taking an SVT decision over accounts on the book; `exposure` is SVT segment-days per reached account over 365.25; `hazard` is expected departures per SVT-account-YEAR of exposure, which is the unit `SVT_INERTIA_ANNUAL_RECENT` is published in.",
  "on_the_three_the_finding_named": "the finding asked for 'the hazard per SVT decision, the size of the SVT population, or the assignment that decides who reaches which route'. On a capture the last two are ONE quantity -- an account reaches the SVT route in a year exactly when it is on the SVT product in that year -- and the factor they leave out is EXPOSURE, how much of the year a reached account spends on the product. So this decomposes the arithmetic three and not the named three.",
