      "2023"
    ]
  },
  "base_window_comparison": {
    "what_this_is": "`svt_inertia_hazard` re-references the published pair by `market_switching_multiplier / svt_inertia_base_multiplier()`. That divisor is the MEAN of the multiplier over `SVT_INERTIA_BASE_WINDOW`, so the factor is 1.0 ACROSS the window and not within each of its years -- see `re_referencing_factor` per year below. Inside the window the world runs the published rate to within a few per cent; everywhere else the factor is 0.56 to 0.90 and a ratio quoted against the published rate would be measuring the re-referencing instead of the source. Both ratios are given because they differ, and quoting one as the other is how two correct figures become a quantity that is not one.",
